# .wave-close-allowlist — known untracked WIP files exempted from the
# `[2/8]` untracked-source-code sentinel in `make wave-close-check`.
#
# One glob or literal path per line. `#` starts a comment (rest of
# line ignored); blank lines are ignored. Entries are matched against
# `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` output, so glob patterns
# (`*`, `?`, `[...]`) are expanded the same way git pathspecs are.
#
# Growth of this file is a reviewer scope-check item (AGENTS.md ->
# Wave-Close Checklist): each entry should have an operator
# disposition tracked in docs/handoff/CURRENT.md or HISTORY.md.
# Unbounded growth here defeats the sentinel's forgotten-`git add`
# purpose — do not add entries casually.

